            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0337" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6038: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-14T17:00:00+08:00">March 14, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 14—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>249. American Consul General Tientsin informed me by telephone today that
                    Japanese have filed another protest with chairman of Hopei Provincial
                    Government, General Yu Hsueh-chung, against stationing of troops and
                    entrenchments in neighborhood of Tientsin and near Tangku as a violation of the
                    Boxer protocol.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
